invariant: INV-11
file: hkdf.c
catches: unit
reason: hmac_sha256 hashes a key of exactly one block, 64 bytes, though
  RFC 2104 section 2 hashes only a key longer than the block. Every HMAC
  under a 64-byte key would then be wrong, and no Finished, binder or
  PSK would match a peer's. The 64-byte boundary row objects.

--- old
    if (key_len > SHA256_BLOCK) {
--- new
    if (key_len >= SHA256_BLOCK) {
